er.type/text] [:db/add "answer:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III/true" :answer/value "true"] [:db/ensure "answer:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III/true" :answer/validate] [:db/add "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III" :answer-field/id #uuid "20cf0325-ce58-53c4-8289-6051883b9317"] [:db/add "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=-2$"] [:db/add "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox] [:db/add "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III" :answer-field/choices "answer:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III/false"] [:db/add "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III" :answer-field/choices "answer:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III/true"] [:db/add "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III" :answer-field/correct "answer:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III/false"] [:db/ensure "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add 17592186600837 :question/answer-fields "field:q-48736/authored-checkbox-v1/III"] [:db/retract 17592186600837 :question/answer-fields 17592186600778] [:db/cas 17592186600837 :question/problem "![](images/36/36477ec421ff4b7f349a060df762eadee83b008fbfc9e021a8893cc45e405cae.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. $f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=-2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=-2$" "![](images/36/36477ec421ff4b7f349a060df762eadee83b008fbfc9e021a8893cc45e405cae.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186600837 :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=-2$ since $f(-2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough  to $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a sharp edge at $x=-2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(-2)$ does not exist.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." "Let's check our statements.\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=2$” is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)=0.$\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=-2$” is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=-2$ since $f(-2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough  to $x=-2.$\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=-2$” is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a sharp edge at $x=-2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(-2)$ does not exist.\n\nTherefore, select “$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=2$” and “$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=-2$.”"] [:db/ensure 17592186600837 :question/validate] [:db/add "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/false" :answer/id #uuid "4390d4ea-941a-5b8d-a336-28415f43f0f9"] [:db/add "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/false" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/false" :answer/value "false"] [:db/ensure "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/false" :answer/validate] [:db/add "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/true" :answer/id #uuid "d2fb8bc7-115b-5bb7-8aa3-3ca8a7a758e2"] [:db/add "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/true" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/true" :answer/value "true"] [:db/ensure "answer:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A/true" :answer/validate] [:db/add "field:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A" :answer-field/id #uuid "de553731-6244-5225-8ef8-b9d0580664d1"] [:db/add "field:q-47693/authored-checkbox-v1/A" :answer-fi